{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be part of your care team while you're here. Can I sit down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I guess."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand you came in after having some thoughts about driving into a tree. Can you tell me more about what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was driving, and suddenly I just felt so heavy. I thought… maybe if I didn’t stop, it would all end. But I did stop. I called my psychiatrist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I'm really glad you did. That took courage. You're not alone in this. We're going to keep you safe while you're here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to hurt myself. But sometimes the depression just… takes over."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. You’ve been through a lot. I see you’ve been on ECT before and it’s helped. Psychiatry is setting that up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it helps. But my veins are terrible. They always have trouble starting IVs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s actually why we’re planning a port-a-cath. It’s a small device placed under the skin that makes it easier to give treatments like ECT without poking your veins each time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is that safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a common procedure. It’s done under local anesthesia, and we’ll make sure you’re comfortable. It’s scheduled for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. That sounds better than getting stuck every time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We also started you on lithium last night—150 mg at bedtime. Psychiatry wants to increase it to help stabilize your mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken lithium before. Does it have side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some people feel a little shaky or thirsty at first. We’ll check your levels and kidney function regularly to keep it safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll watch for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night look stable. White blood cell count is normal, thyroid is fine. We’re still waiting on the lithium level to confirm it’s in range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the methadone in my urine test a problem? I haven’t taken any."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. The test did show methadone, but you’re not on it. We’ll document that you deny use. It could be a false positive or contamination, but we’ll keep it on record."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want anyone thinking I’m using drugs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. Your history shows you’ve been sober since pregnancy. We trust your word and will note that clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-09-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a heads-up—the port-a-cath procedure is set for noon. You’ll be given medication to relax, and the team will place it in your chest. It’ll be covered with a dressing after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-09-05 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-09-05 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll feel some pressure, but not sharp pain. The area will be numbed. Afterward, there might be some soreness, like after any minor surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-09-05 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m nervous, but I want this to work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-09-05 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The port-a-cath was placed successfully. The X-ray shows the line is in the right spot, near your heart. You did great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-09-05 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it… inside my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-09-05 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tip is in a large vein near the heart—perfect for safe delivery of medications. It’s not in the heart muscle. You’ll barely notice it once healed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-09-05 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the site feeling? Any redness or pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s a little tender, but not bad. I can move my arm okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That’s normal. We’ll keep the dressing dry and change it in a couple of days. No lifting more than 10 pounds for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, psychiatry wants to increase your lithium to 300 mg at bedtime. We’ll check your level again tomorrow to make sure it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-09-06 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll take it as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-09-07 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your lithium level came back at 0.3, which is a bit low. That’s why we increased the dose. It may take a few days to rise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-09-07 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it help with the suicidal thoughts?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-09-07 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can help stabilize your mood over time. Combined with ECT, it gives you the best chance to feel better. You’re not on this alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-09-07 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-09-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood count is improving—hemoglobin up from 11.2 to 12.2. That’s good. Everything else looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-09-08 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of the B12 deficiency?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-09-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. You’re on a multivitamin now, which includes B12. We’ll keep an eye on it, but it’s not urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-09-08 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-09-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatric team saw you this morning. They said your mood is more stable, and you’re denying current suicidal thoughts. That’s progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-09-09 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel down, but not like last week. I think the ECT will help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-09-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling your first ECT session for Friday. You’ll be asleep during it, and you’ll wake up in recovery. Most people feel tired afterward, but not in pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-09-09 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from before. I just hope it works again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-09-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your port site is healing well—just mild swelling and tenderness. No signs of infection. You can start gentle arm movements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-09-10 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-09-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’re here to support you through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-09-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Big day tomorrow—your first ECT. You’ll be taken to the procedure room, given anesthesia, and it’ll be over in minutes. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-09-11 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I remember anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-09-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’ll be fully asleep. Some people have short-term memory gaps, but it usually improves. The team will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-09-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m ready to try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-09-12 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. You did great with ECT today. You woke up alert, and your vitals are stable. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-09-12 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired. A little confused, but it’s clearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-09-12 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. You’ll rest here for a bit, then we’ll get you ready for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re being transferred to Deaconess 4, an inpatient psychiatric unit, for continued ECT and care. You’ll stay there for a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m a little nervous, but I know I need this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s okay to feel that way. You’ve made real progress. You’re safer, your mood is more stable, and you’re taking steps toward healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. For listening. For not judging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. You’re doing hard work, and we’re proud of you. Keep going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-09-12 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Your mom will be here soon to go with you. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-09-04 16:46:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-09-12 19:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman was admitted after reporting suicidal ideation involving a plan to drive into a tree, following a history of bipolar disorder and prior suicide attempts. She was placed under observation with a 1:1 sitter and admitted for monitoring while awaiting electroconvulsive therapy (ECT). Due to poor venous access, a port-a-cath was successfully placed on hospital day 4, with imaging confirming proper placement. Lithium was initiated and titrated to 300 mg nightly for mood stabilization. She remained medically stable throughout her stay, denied active suicidal ideation at discharge, and underwent her first ECT session on the final day. She was discharged to an inpatient psychiatric facility for continuation of ECT and psychiatric care.",
    "problems": [
      "Bipolar disorder, current episode depressed, severe, without psychotic features",
      "Hypotension, unspecified",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Chronic pain syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
